2026-10-02  Chris Burdess  <dog@gnu.org>

	Release 1.0.1.

	Parity with javac on gumdrop (1408 sources, 552 JUnit test sources):
	everything compiles and the JUnit suite passes.  The individual fixes
	are recorded in the git history between v1.0.0 and this release.
	* src/semantic.c: Generic method return inference, method type
	parameters, parameterized interface inheritance, overload resolution
	(boxing and widening priorities, inaccessible and bridge methods of
	class-file classes), varargs across files, imports (wildcard, single-
	type before same-package, nested types), annotation retention,
	captures in lambdas and nested local classes, -sourcepath loading.
	* src/codegen.c, src/codegen_expr.c, src/codegen_stmt.c,
	src/stackmap.c: Stack map frames for try/finally, try-with-resources,
	switch, synchronized and loops; boxing and unboxing; primitive casts;
	enum and string switch labels; enum constant bodies, nested annotation
	types, anonymous class constructors, synthetic accessors for inherited
	protected fields, NestMembers at every depth.
	* src/classwriter.c, src/lexer.c, src/parser.c: Unicode escapes and
	supplementary characters in string literals; "final" catch parameters;
	nested class access flags.
	* src/genesis.c (compile_parallel, compile_batch): Restart the batch
	with the source files loaded through -sourcepath added to it.
	* bench/compare-compilers.sh, bench/gumdrop-ant-test.sh: New.  "make
	bench" and "make gumdrop-smoke".

	Performance.
	* src/semantic.c (symbol_from_classfile_shared, external_class_import)
	(symbol_from_classfile_impl): New.  Build the symbol of a class file
	once per batch and replay its effect on each analyzer's type cache.
	(semantic_prebuild_external_classes): New.  Build them before the
	worker processes are forked.
	(type_registry_ensure_indexes, type_registry_nested_entries)
	(type_registry_entries_by_simple_name): New.  Index the registry by
	outer type and by simple name.
	(registry_lookup_nested_members, load_external_class_impl): Use the
	indexes in place of walks over every registered type.
	(load_external_class): Remember qualified names that do not exist.
	(type_registry_seal, type_registry_lookup): No lock once registration
	is over.
	(resolve_type_name_with_imports, resolve_types_in_compilation_unit_cached):
	Resolve each simple name once per file; remember classpath and
	sourcepath probes per thread.
	(resolve_unresolved_type): Remember qualified names per class while
	its members are entered.
	(find_best_method_by_types): Type each argument once, not once per
	candidate.
	* src/classpath.c (classpath_build_package_index, classpath_dir_files):
	New.  Go straight to the archives holding a package; list a package
	directory once.
	(classpath_find_class): Use them.  Do not remember names in packages
	that do not exist.
	(jar_read_entry): Positioned reads; safe for concurrent readers.
	(classpath_loaded_class_names): New.
	* src/genesis.c (compile_with_worker_processes, worker_process_run):
	New.  Semantic analysis and code generation in worker processes.
	(qualify_phase_worker): New.  Qualify type names on threads.
	(analyze_file, generate_file_code): New, from compile_batch and
	codegen_phase_worker.
	(output_class): No global lock for directory output; plain open, write
	and close; create directories only when missing.
	(timing_mark): New.  GENESIS_DEBUG_TIMING, GENESIS_DEBUG_PAUSE.
	* src/util.c (intern_len, intern, intern_init, intern_cleanup): Sharded
	table with storage that never moves.
	(intern_set_concurrent): New.
	(debug_env_init): New.
	* src/util.h (debug_getenv): New.  All GENESIS_DEBUG_* tests use it.
	* src/lexer.c (lookup_keyword): Dismiss non-keywords on the first
	character.
	* src/constpool.c (cp_add_class): Find the class entry by name index.

	Class files loaded in any order.
	* src/semantic.c (load_member_class_file): New.  Load a member class by
	way of its outer class.
	(load_external_class): Answer a load of a class that is still loading
	its nested types from the type cache.
	(symbol_from_classfile_impl): Give a nested class cached before its
	outer class its simple name and enclosing class.
	(get_expression_type): Load the symbol of a field's type before
	looking a further field up in it.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (codegen_field_access): Resolve an inherited field
	as the receiver in this.field.other.

	Data races in code generation on threads.
	* src/semantic.c (load_external_class_impl): Do not store a registry
	type's symbol pointer when it already has that value.
	* src/codegen.c (generate_interface_bridges): Do not store the resolved
	return type in the shared interface method symbol.

	* Makefile.am (EXTRA_DIST): README is now README.md.
	* README.md, CONTRIBUTING, NEWS: Updated.

2026-09-27  Chris Burdess  <dog@gnu.org>

	Release 1.0.0.

	Build system: GNU Autoconf and Automake.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.am, src/Makefile.am, m4/: New.  Require C99,
	zlib and POSIX threads; pin -std=c99; WARN_CFLAGS for -Wall -Wextra
	-pedantic.  The old hand-written Makefile is removed.
	* AUTHORS, NEWS, ChangeLog, README, CONTRIBUTING: New or updated for the
	GNU layout.  README.md is now README.
	* test/: Regression tests, jtreg glue (test/fake-jdk) and the test driver
	test/run-tests.sh.  Development only; not in EXTRA_DIST, so not in the
	distribution tarball.  "make check", "make check-one TEST=...",
	"make jtreg-test".
	* src/*.c: Include <config.h> first.
	* src/genesis.h (GENESIS_VERSION): Take the version from configure.ac.
	* src/genesis.c (shared_counter_t): Replace C11 atomics with a
	mutex-protected counter.
	(print_version, print_usage): Print package name, bug address.
	(main): Accept --version and --help.

	Class file version and -target.
	* src/genesis.c (compiler_options_new): -target defaults to unset
	(automatic).
	(codegen_phase_worker): Set the target version on the top-level class
	before it is generated and written; previously only nested, local and
	anonymous classes received it.
	* src/classwriter.c (choose_class_version): New.  Compute the lowest
	version the class needs (floor 52); treat an explicit target as a
	ceiling and report an error when a feature needs more.  Omit the
	NestHost/NestMembers attributes for explicit targets below 55.
	* src/codegen.h (class_gen_t): Add is_record.
	* src/codegen.c (codegen_class): Set it.  The old ACC_RECORD test was
	dead code, so records never raised the class file version.

	Lambdas, method references and generics.
	* src/codegen.c (inner_class_access_flags): New.  Build InnerClasses
	flags including ACC_INTERFACE, ACC_ABSTRACT, ACC_ENUM, ACC_ANNOTATION
	and implicit static.  Used for the three kinds of InnerClasses entry
	here and in src/codegen_stmt.c.
	* src/semantic.c (get_functional_interface_sam): Make public.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (codegen_expr): Use it for method references
	instead of a private single-abstract-method counter.
	* src/semantic.c (preregister_nested_types): Declare a nested class's
	own type parameters before resolving its member signatures; the later
	pass reuses those symbols so the class and its members share one type
	variable.
	* src/semantic.c (symbol_from_classfile): Give a bare type-variable
	field the bound implied by its descriptor.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (codegen_method_call): Treat a field of type-
	variable type as a receiver, dispatching on its bound.
	(coerce_arg_to_param): New.  Shared argument conversion (boxing,
	unboxing, widening) extracted from codegen_method_call.
	(codegen_new_object): Convert constructor arguments with it; use the
	descriptor stored in a class file for external constructors; count
	stack slots from the declared parameter types.
	(checkcast_generic_field): New.  Cast a type-variable field read back
	to its specific type.

	String concatenation and anonymous classes.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (get_append_descriptor): Trust the resolved type
	first; append wrappers and other references as Object.
	(codegen_string_concat): Take the argument slot count from the append
	overload chosen, not from the operand's unboxed kind.
	(codegen_method_call): Compute the argument slot count once, from the
	parameter types, before emitting the call; use it for the invokeinterface
	count operand.
	* src/semantic.c (declared_inside_current_class): New.  Do not treat a
	parameter or local of a local/anonymous class's own method as captured.
	* src/codegen.c (codegen_anonymous_class): Generate superclass and
	interface bridge methods, as codegen_class does.
	* test/src/java8/{StringConcatBoxedTest,AnonymousParamTest}.java: New.

	Diagnostics.
	* src/parser.c (parser_parse): Report, and stop at, an
	unrecognised top-level declaration instead of discarding the error.
	Give a specific message for records and sealed classes below the
	source level that supports them.
	* src/genesis.c (output_class): Drop a redundant error message.

	Tests.
	* test/run-tests.sh: Precompile helper classes for every version
	directory; add class file version, -target ceiling, old -source,
	invalid input and class-file-loaded generic class checks.
	* test/classversion/, test/oldsource/, test/external/,
	test/invalid/StrayTopLevelMember.java,
	test/src/java8/{NestedGenericTest,BoundedTypeVarCallTest,
	TypeVarBoxingTest}.java: New.

	Primitive conversions: widening, boxing, unboxing, promotion.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (emit_widen_primitive, coerce_stack_value,
	descriptor_kind_and_class, value_kind_and_class,
	coerce_value_to_descriptor): New, in codegen_internal.h so
	codegen_stmt.c can use them too.  Applied at every local variable
	declaration and simple assignment (local, static and instance field
	via a bare name, an inherited field, a field in an enclosing class, or
	"obj.field", and array element), at every field declaration
	initializer (codegen.c), and to a return statement's value against
	the method's (or, for a lambda, the SAM's) declared return type.
	(codegen_compound_rhs): New, replacing emit_compound_op (deleted) at
	every compound-assignment site listed above.  Generates the
	right-hand side, applies binary numeric promotion between the
	left-hand side's own type and the right's (an int-only shift count
	for <<=/>>=/>>>=, never promoted), emits the correctly-typed operator,
	and narrows the result back to the left-hand side's type (JLS
	15.26.2); a String left-hand side with += concatenates via a
	StringBuilder instead; a boxed numeric left-hand side is unboxed and
	reboxed around the same logic.
	(codegen_binary_expr): Fix the operand/result slot count at the end,
	wrong for a long or double result since it assumed one slot
	regardless of operand width. Exempt a shift's right operand from
	being widened to the left operand's promoted type, which is not
	valid input for LSHL/LSHR/LUSHR; select the shift opcode from the
	left operand's type alone.
	(codegen_assignment, AST_CONDITIONAL_EXPR): Apply the same numeric
	promotion between a ternary's two branches that a binary operator's
	operands get, needed for a consistent stack map at their merge point.
	* src/codegen_stmt.c (AST_VAR_DECL, AST_RETURN_STMT): Use the new
	helpers instead of a narrower, boxing/unboxing-only check.
	* src/semantic.c (pass2_check_types): Persist sem_type on
	AST_BINARY_EXPR, AST_UNARY_EXPR and AST_CONDITIONAL_EXPR nodes, as
	already done for AST_FIELD_ACCESS and AST_METHOD_CALL; several codegen
	heuristics (including overload-sensitive descriptor selection, e.g.
	for println) already checked for this and silently fell back to
	guessing without it.
	(get_expression_type, AST_CONDITIONAL_EXPR): Apply the same numeric
	promotion JLS 15.25 gives a ternary's branches that a binary
	operator's operands get, instead of returning the "then" branch's
	type unconditionally.
	* src/parser.c (parser_classify_gt_sequence): New, replacing
	parser_check_double_gt/parser_check_triple_gt (deleted). Fix >>=
	and >>>= being silently dropped, with no error and no bytecode: the
	lexer never combines '>' into >>/>>>, to keep a generic argument
	list simple, but does still combine a lone '>' with an immediately
	following '=' into one token, same as everywhere else; the old
	reconstruction assumed a separate trailing '=' token it would never
	find, since the *last* '>' of the run absorbs it first.
	(parser_consume_gt_sequence): New, replacing
	parser_consume_double_gt/parser_consume_triple_gt (deleted).
	* test/src/java8/{PrimitiveWideningTest,CompoundAssignmentTest,
	BinaryPromotionTest}.java: New.

	Assignment through an explicit receiver.
	* src/codegen_expr.c (codegen_assignment, obj.field = x and
	Test.sfield = x): DUP_X1/DUP2_X1 (receiver case) or DUP/DUP2 (static,
	by class name) the stored value so the assignment expression can be
	used as a sub-expression, as every identifier-target case already
	could. Add compound-assignment support (via codegen_compound_rhs) to
	the by-class-name static case, which had none at all.
	* test/src/java8/FieldAssignChainTest.java: New.

	Record toString() simple name.
	* src/codegen.c (codegen_class, record toString()): Take the class
	name from class_sym->name (already the simple name) instead of
	parsing it out of internal_name by stripping up to the last '/'.
	That left the enclosing class's name in place for a nested record,
	whose only separator from its own simple name is '$', not '/'
	("Outer$Point[x=1]" instead of "Point[x=1]").
	* test/src/java16/NestedRecordToStringTest.java: New.

